{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merge reference: name the successor when retiring an artifact, and the two rename cases.\n\nSuccessor at this path for head 66bf2404, answering review's findings 2 and 3. Bare supersession is no longer offered as the ordinary move; it is now stated as the deletion case alone, because a supersession that cites its replacement says \"moved here\" and one that does not says \"gone\", and the difference is what a reader following the chain runs into. The rename row is split, since a rename can land on an occupied path and the previous text assumed it never did.\n\nThe page's own frontmatter is repaired too. It rested on a retired cmd/gs/main.go artifact and on a branch-slug path that can never be superseded — a page about succession, anchored to something incapable of it. It now rests on the live cmd/gs/main.go artifact, where the merge guard it documents actually lives.\n\nThis retires two predecessors at this exact path: the artifact for a4f4a57a, and the one for 7b5c0701 which was published without retiring it. That omission is the rule this page states, missed on the page itself.\n\n`go vet ./...` clean and `go test ./internal/docset -count=1` passes at this head. The docset gate executes the examples rather than reading them, so the corrected flag order is verified.","body":{"commit":"66bf24046b4f4a466dedaabdf06896497f708375","path":"docs/reference/gs/merge.md"}}